{
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 proof that symmetric informationally complete POVMs (SIC-POVMs) exist in every finite dimension. The compared statement is OpenQuantumProblem23.sicPOVMs from google-deepmind/formal-conjectures, the existence form of Open Quantum Problem 23 and of Zauner's conjecture: for every d >= 1 there are d^2 unit vectors in C^d whose pairwise squared overlaps all equal 1/(d+1). The configuration also compares the eleven benchmark theorems of the same file, which state the cases d = 56, 58, 59, 60, 64, 68, 69, 70, 71, 72 and 75. The mathematics is due to Radchenko and Wheeler, who build the required vectors from special values of the modular quantum dilogarithm and show by class field theory that a suitable Galois automorphism exists, together with the reduction of Appleby, Flammia and Kopp from such \"ghost\" vectors to SIC-POVMs. The Lean proof follows the argument of these sources in five parts: the reduction to a ghost fiducial with a unimodular Galois flip, the finite identities for the special values, their algebraicity by a 2-adic argument, the analytic properties of Faddeev's quantum dilogarithm, and the reciprocity argument through ray class fields, Artin reciprocity and the Chebotarev density theorem. Class field theory comes from the external Lean library of N. Yamaguchi and the Chebotarev density theorem from a vendored, ported copy of the library of C. Birkbeck. The repository also proves, as a further result outside the compared configuration, the existence of rank-r SICs of Appleby, Flammia and Kopp for r >= 1, d > 2r + 1 and r(d - r) dividing d^2 - 1. All proofs depend only on propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound, and no sorry remains outside the deliberate placeholders of the Challenge. An earlier, independent Lean formalization of SIC existence by Māris Ozols exists, with its own statements.",
